Lemma~\ref{lem:pointfiber}. Let $\widehat J$ be a smooth tame almost
complex structure on $M$. Then there is a smooth tame $J$ on $M$ with
\[
\phi_i\circ J=i\,\phi_i\ \text{ on } X\ (i\le r),
\qquad
J=\widehat J\ \text{ on }\ M\setminus X' ,
\]
where $X'\Supset X$ is a slightly larger ball. Moreover, if $\widehat
J$ already satisfies the constraints on a closed subset $C\subset X$,
one can take $J=\widehat J$ on an open set slightly smaller than $C$
shrunk... precisely: given open $C_\circ$ with $\overline{C_\circ}
\subset\{q\in X:\widehat J(q)\text{ satisfies the constraints at }
q\}$, one can arrange $J=\widehat J$ on $\overline{C_\circ}$.
\end{lemma}

